-- title:
--   Deligne-Drinfeld-Ihara conjecture: $\mathfrak{grt}_1$ is free on $\sigma_3, \sigma_5, \sigma_7, \dots$
-- statement:
--   **Conjecture (Deligne, Drinfeld, Ihara).** The graded Grothendieck-Teichmüller Lie algebra $\mathfrak{grt}_1$ is the free Lie algebra, for the Ihara bracket, on a family of generators $\sigma_3, \sigma_5, \sigma_7, \dots$, one in each odd degree at least $3$.
--
--   Formally: there exists a family $(\sigma_p)_{p\ge0}$ with $\sigma_p \in \mathfrak{grt}_1$ homogeneous of degree $2p+3$, such that the Lie algebra morphism
--
--   $$\mathbb F(\mathbb N) \longrightarrow \mathrm{Der}, \qquad p \longmapsto D_{\sigma_p},$$
--
--   out of the free Lie algebra on countably many generators is injective and has image exactly $D(\mathfrak{grt}_1) = \{ D_\psi : \psi \in \mathfrak{grt}_1 \}$. Here $D_f$ is the Ihara derivation attached to $f$, and $\mathrm{Der}$ is the Lie algebra of derivations of $\mathbb F(x,y)$ with the commutator bracket; passing to derivations is a faithful way of recording the Ihara bracket on $\mathfrak{grt}_1$, since $[D_f,D_g] = D_{\{f,g\}}$ and $f \mapsto D_f$ is injective on $\mathfrak{grt}_1$.
--
--   The existence and non-vanishing of suitable $\sigma_p$ is known (Drinfeld), and injectivity - freeness of the subalgebra they generate - is a theorem of F. Brown. What is open is surjectivity: that $\mathfrak{grt}_1$ contains nothing beyond the Lie algebra generated by these elements. Equivalently, the dimension of $\mathfrak{grt}_1$ in each degree would be determined, and the pro-unipotent Grothendieck-Teichmüller group described by free generators.
-- source:
--   Thomas Willwacher, The Grothendieck-Teichmüller Group, ETH Zürich lecture notes (in progress), 27 February 2014, Section 5.1, p. 49, Corollary 5.2 and the following paragraph (Deligne-Drinfeld-Ihara conjecture: grt_1 is the completed free Lie algebra generated by sigma_{2p+1}, p = 1, 2, 3, ...)

import Definitions.Def_GT_grt1

namespace GrothendieckTeichmuller

theorem deligne_drinfeld_ihara :
    ∃ sigma : ℕ → Lxy,
      (∀ p, sigma p ∈ grt1 ∧ IsHomogeneousOfDegree (2 * p + 3) (sigma p)) ∧
      Function.Injective ⇑(FreeLieAlgebra.lift ℚ (fun p : ℕ => iharaDeriv (sigma p))) ∧
      Set.range ⇑(FreeLieAlgebra.lift ℚ (fun p : ℕ => iharaDeriv (sigma p))) =
        iharaDeriv '' (grt1 : Set Lxy) := by sorry

end GrothendieckTeichmuller
